Southern U.S. cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Bread|Bread]]\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|Vegetable oil]] for [[Cookbook:Fry|frying]]\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Cornmeal|yellow corn meal]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Flour|all-purpose flour]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* 1¾ teaspoons [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]], [[Cookbook:Beat|lightly beaten]]\n* ⅛ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Chop|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Green Onion|green onions]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Pour oil 3–4 inches (7.5 cm to 10 cm) deep in a pan and preheat to [[Cookbook:Oven temperatures|370°F]] (~190°C).\n# In bowl mix cornmeal, flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt, and cayenne.\n# Mix in eggs, green onions, milk, and ¼ cup vegetable oil.\n# Spoon 6–7 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] of the batter into preheated oil.\n# Fry, stirring constantly for overall browning, until golden brown.\n# Remove from heat and drain on [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|paper towels]].\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* ⅓ cup [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Green Onion|green onions]] may be substituted for fresh onions.\n* Add 6 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] (170 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]])  pimento cheese to the batter.\n\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Deep fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for fritters]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornmeal]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\